1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,325
A campaign is a named push of work, such as a spring lead drive.

2
00:00:05,325 --> 00:00:10,454
This video shows why campaigns and campaign groups exist, how to create them,

3
00:00:10,454 --> 00:00:14,100
and where they are used by loads, agents and reports.

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:22,314
Calling, texting and follow-up work needs a name.

5
00:00:22,314 --> 00:00:28,490
Without one, a report cannot tell a spring lead drive from a round of renewal reminders.

6
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:32,728
For the outbound dialer, the name matters even more.

7
00:00:32,728 --> 00:00:37,540
Agents sign in to a campaign to receive the dialer calls of that campaign.

8
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:40,685
Related campaigns can be rolled up.

9
00:00:40,685 --> 00:00:45,242
A campaign group shows several campaigns as one line in reports, such as

10
00:00:45,242 --> 00:00:47,170
every campaign of a season.

11
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,768
A campaign only groups and reports work.

12
00:00:50,768 --> 00:00:56,340
It does not choose the channel, the number used, or what happens after each outcome.

13
00:01:00,586 --> 00:01:04,280
Open Interaction Center, Management, Campaign Groups.

14
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,908
A group is optional.

15
00:01:05,908 --> 00:01:10,666
If you want to roll campaigns up in reports, click Add campaign group.

16
00:01:11,156 --> 00:01:15,256
Enter a Name and an optional Description, then click Save.

17
00:01:15,256 --> 00:01:19,676
The group appears in the list, ready to be picked by campaigns.

18
00:01:23,905 --> 00:01:28,825
Open Campaigns, in the same Management menu, and click Add Campaign.

19
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:36,509
Enter a Name.

20
00:01:36,509 --> 00:01:39,966
Pick a Campaign group, or leave No campaign group.

21
00:01:39,966 --> 00:01:44,596
Add an optional Description, so people know what the campaign is for.

22
00:01:47,685 --> 00:01:48,698
Click Save.

23
00:01:48,698 --> 00:01:53,705
The campaign appears in the list, with its name and the person who created it.

24
00:01:54,243 --> 00:01:58,043
A second campaign, Renewal reminders, has no group.

25
00:01:58,043 --> 00:02:02,043
It is added the same way, and the list now shows both.

26
00:02:03,951 --> 00:02:10,498
Campaigns and campaign groups cannot be deleted, because activities and reports keep pointing at them.

27
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:16,621
Moving a campaign to another group also changes how its past activities are grouped in reports.

28
00:02:20,852 --> 00:02:25,466
Agents sign in only to the campaigns on their entitlements.

29
00:02:25,466 --> 00:02:30,932
Open Agent entitlements, click Add, and pick the user, here jamie.chen.

30
00:02:37,496 --> 00:02:41,928
Allowed campaigns lists the campaigns the agent may sign in to.

31
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:43,791
Pick Spring lead drive.

32
00:02:43,791 --> 00:02:48,416
Allowed queues are for inbound work, and are set on the same page.

33
00:02:48,911 --> 00:02:49,926
Click Save.

34
00:02:49,926 --> 00:02:53,809
The agent now sees Spring lead drive in the Work tab of the

35
00:02:53,809 --> 00:02:56,198
soft phone, and can sign in to it.

36
00:02:56,198 --> 00:02:59,901
Removing a campaign here also signs the agent out of it.

37
00:03:04,101 --> 00:03:08,450
A manager creates the campaign, and adds it to the entitlements of the

38
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:09,881
agents who work it.

39
00:03:10,631 --> 00:03:16,051
A dialer load picks the campaign, and creates an activity for each contact in it.

40
00:03:16,801 --> 00:03:20,974
Agents sign in to the campaign in the soft phone, and the dialer

41
00:03:20,974 --> 00:03:22,941
offers or places its calls.

42
00:03:23,691 --> 00:03:28,407
Every call ends with an outcome on its activity, and the reports show

43
00:03:28,407 --> 00:03:31,111
the results by campaign and by group.

44
00:03:35,311 --> 00:03:41,032
On an activity load, the campaign is stamped on every activity the load creates.

45
00:03:41,032 --> 00:03:44,891
Without one, the subject's Default campaign is used.

46
00:03:45,641 --> 00:03:51,005
On a dialer load, the campaign is required, unless the subject has a default one.

47
00:03:51,005 --> 00:03:54,211
It is the line of work that agents sign in to.

48
00:03:54,961 --> 00:04:01,101
On an agent's entitlements, Allowed campaigns lists the campaigns the agent may sign in to.

49
00:04:01,851 --> 00:04:06,535
In reports, the campaign and the campaign group are filters, so you can

50
00:04:06,535 --> 00:04:09,941
see the results of one push, or of a whole season.

51
00:04:14,141 --> 00:04:17,998
One campaign for each push of work, such as a lead drive, a

52
00:04:17,998 --> 00:04:23,161
renewal round or an appointment reminder, keeps the numbers of each easy to read.

53
00:04:23,911 --> 00:04:28,336
A group for each season, region or brand lets a manager see the

54
00:04:28,336 --> 00:04:31,351
total for all of them in one report line.

55
00:04:32,101 --> 00:04:36,374
Calls and texts for the same push can share one campaign, so their

56
00:04:36,374 --> 00:04:38,511
results are reported together.

57
00:04:40,511 --> 00:04:45,001
Name each push of work, group the related ones, and agents, loads and

58
00:04:45,001 --> 00:04:47,694
reports all point to the same campaign.

59
00:04:47,694 --> 00:04:49,251
Thanks for watching.

